<title>BELGIUM: Belgian Immolease 1996 profit grows 12.2 pct.</title>
<headline>Belgian Immolease 1996 profit grows 12.2 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-04-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Immolease, part of the Belgian Almanij-Kredietbank group, said on Thursday that 1996 net profit rose 12.2 percent to 76.8 million francs.</p>
<p>Immolease, which is primarily active in property finance and management, said its shareholders' meeting approved a dividend payout of 28.7 million francs against 26.1 million for 1995.</p>
<p>It added 12 million francs to reserves. Own funds grew by 12.8 percent to 387.3 million francs, after profit distribution.</p>
<p>Immolease said it had been the seventh year in a row that net profit rose more than 12 percent.</p>
<p>-- Bert Lauwers, Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6815.</p>
</text>
